From: Ilya I. Nikitin <ilya.i.nikitin@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:58:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] linking: recompute a stale priority media role link

The highest-priority media role link per target media class is cached
in lutils.priority_media_role_link and cleared only in
unhandleLinkable(), when a linkable goes away. Links removed any other
way - prepare-link moving a stream to a new target, as every card
profile switch does, or a failed media role activation - stay cached.

rescan-media-role-links then applies the dead link's policy to all
live ones. With a dead Alert-role link cached, every new Multimedia
stream is corked: its link is never activated, its ports are never
configured, and it sits suspended with none, while the code after the
loop keeps trying to activate the dead link. Only restarting
WirePlumber cleared it.

Before using the cached link, check that it is still one of the live
role links for the media class, and otherwise let
clearPriorityMediaRoleLink() recompute it from the live ones.

On an msm8939 phone whose card switches between an earpiece and a
speaker profile around every call, playback failed after the first
switch every time; with this, 24 switches in a row each played, and
the cached link was found dead on 23 of them.
---
--- a/src/scripts/linking/rescan-media-role-links.lua
+++ b/src/scripts/linking/rescan-media-role-links.lua
@@ -108,6 +108,28 @@
         local pmrl_active = nil
         pmrl = lutils.getPriorityMediaRoleLink(mc)
 
+        -- The cache is only cleared when a linkable goes away, so a link
+        -- removed any other way can linger in it and cork every stream of a
+        -- lower role. Trust it only while it is still a live link.
+        if pmrl then
+          local live = false
+          for link in om:iterate {
+            type = "SiLink",
+            Constraint { "is.role.policy.link", "=", true },
+            Constraint { "target.media.class", "=", mc },
+          } do
+            if link == pmrl then
+              live = true
+              break
+            end
+          end
+          if not live then
+            log:info("priority media role link is gone, recomputing")
+            lutils.clearPriorityMediaRoleLink(pmrl)
+            pmrl = lutils.getPriorityMediaRoleLink(mc)
+          end
+        end
+
         log:debug("Rescanning media role links...")
 
         local function onMediaRoleLinkActivated (l, e)
